  {
   "id": "h1",
   "scene": "hook",
   "start": 2,
   "len": 65,
   "text": "Your pre-workout is mostly one thing."
  },
  {
   "id": "h2",
   "scene": "hook",
   "start": 70,
   "len": 48,
   "text": "Caffeine. Here's how to use it right."
  },
  {
   "id": "w1",
   "scene": "works",
   "start": 143,
   "len": 157,
   "text": "Does it work? A meta-analysis says yes. A small but real boost in strength and power."
  },
  {
   "id": "d1",
   "scene": "dose",
   "start": 323,
   "len": 146,
   "text": "The research dose: three to six milligrams per kilo, about sixty minutes before you train."
  },
  {
   "id": "d2",
   "scene": "dose",
   "start": 472,
   "len": 105,
   "text": "For an eighty kilo lifter, the low end is about two coffees."
  },
  {
   "id": "d3",
   "scene": "dose",
   "start": 580,
   "len": 150,
   "text": "And more isn't better. Around nine milligrams per kilo brings side effects, with no extra gains."
  },
  {
   "id": "l1",
   "scene": "limit",
   "start": 743,
   "len": 137,
   "text": "Daily ceiling for healthy adults: four hundred milligrams. Pregnant? Two hundred."
  },
  {
   "id": "z1",
   "scene": "sleep",
   "start": 893,
   "len": 100,
   "text": "The catch is sleep. Have your coffee at least nine hours before bed."
  },
  {
   "id": "z2",
   "scene": "sleep",
   "start": 996,
   "len": 64,
   "text": "A pre-workout scoop? About thirteen."
  },
  {
   "id": "x1",
   "scene": "health",
   "start": 1073,
   "len": 115,
   "text": "The good news: three to four cups a day is linked to a lower risk of early death."
  },
  {
   "id": "x2",
   "scene": "health",
   "start": 1191,
   "len": 29,
   "text": "Linked, not proven."
  },
  {
   "id": "e1",
   "scene": "bridge",
   "start": 1234,
   "len": 54,
   "text": "Caffeine fuels the session."
  },
  {
   "id": "e2",
   "scene": "bridge",
